{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310852,"nonce":"OkSfb2zV9MVv5sFG0KiXGqMzVHY=","title":"The Candle-like ML framework being built on top of Rayzor (LLM inference, edge-first) ships as `nue.*` — not `rayzor.nn.*`. Named after the ...","message":"The ML framework / NN layer being built on Rayzor is called **`nue`** (after the yōkai/mononoke). It is its own top-level Haxe package, alongside but not under `rayzor.*`.\n\n**Why:** User directive (2026-05-18) while planning the Candle-like ML framework. `nue` is the framework name (parallel to PyTorch's `nn`, candle, tch). Keeping it top-level signals it as an independent library that happens to be powered by Rayzor's runtime, not a sub-module of Rayzor itself.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- New ML packages: `nue.Module`, `nue.Linear`, `nue.Embedding`, `nue.transformer.*` (GQAttention, RoPE, KVCache, SwiGLU, TransformerBlock, Llama), `nue.tokenizer.*` (BPE), `nue.sampling.*` (argmax, top-k, top-p, temperature), `nue.loader.GGUF`, etc.\n- Do NOT put any of this under `rayzor.nn.*` or `rayzor.ml.*`.\n- Foundation primitives stay under rayzor: `rayzor.ds.Tensor`, `rayzor.ds.Device`, `rayzor.ds.DType`, `rayzor.concurrent.NumaPool`, `rayzor.gpu.*`. The framework `nue` consumes these.\n- Native runtime functions stay rayzor-prefixed (`rayzor_tensor_*`, `rayzor_numa_*`) — `nue` is a Haxe-layer namespace only.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_nue_ml_framework` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}